--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications made by this project
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Build system: the reference builds its client bundle with tsdown and copies
   `lib/index.iife.js`; this project builds the same sources with rollup into
   `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })` CJS form (tools/build-client.mjs).
2. Settings transport: DSH 0.2.1 no longer provides `ctx.settingsScope`, so
   `packages/dsh-fairy-visual/src/client/scope-shim.js` supplies the same
   `getSnapshot()/subscribe()/set()` surface over a host HTTP route
   (`GET/PUT /dsh-fairy/settings?ns=<namespace>`) backed by JSON files in
   `$DSH_HOME/fairy-visual/` and `$DSH_HOME/fairy-identity/`.
3. Host halves (`src/index.js`): the reference registers settings through the
   0.1.1 `settings` service; here each package registers its own `webServer`
   route instead. Voice paths and the balance-meter credentials path now honour
   `DSH_HOME` / `DSH_FAIRY_CREDENTIALS`.
4. DOM compatibility for DSH 0.2.1 in `packages/dsh-fairy-visual/src/client/dom-adapter.js`:
   `conversation` also matches `[data-slot="main.conversation"]`,
   `composerTextarea` also matches `[data-composer-input]` (0.2.1 uses a
   contenteditable div instead of a textarea), and `phaseActive` stays
   `[data-phase="active"]` because the composer input carries its own
   `data-phase` vocabulary (`plain`).
5. `dsh-fairy-startup` tolerates the missing `sessions.clear()` in 0.2.1 instead
   of failing the whole client graph.
6. Relative contract imports are rewritten to `../../../dsh-fairy-contracts/`.
7. Added tooling that the reference does not ship: `tools/build-client.mjs`,
   `tools/build-all.mjs`, `tools/verify-build.mjs`, `tools/port-packages.mjs`,
   `tools/dev-*.mjs`, `tools/cdp/**` (CDP parity/contrast/DOM audits),
   `dev/profile/**` (isolated dev profile).
8. Session selection source: the reference reads
   `sessions.list.getSnapshot().current`, which no longer exists in 0.2.1 (the
   snapshot only carries `ids`/`byId`/`phase`/`projectionsBySession`), so the
   handover never fired and activity stayed `normal`. `session-source.js` reads
   `uiSession.current` instead and falls back to the sessions store.
9. Model-picker stacking: the mascot animation-speed rail is an invisible
   `input[type=range]` spanning the same band as the native model button and
   swallowed every click. The reference reproduces this overlap, so the fix here
   is a stacking change only (the picker is lifted above the rail; geometry is
   untouched).
10. Model-picker ownership: the reference clones the native model control and
    hides the original (`-native-` marker). 0.2.1 exposes a single node carrying
    both markers, which the hide rule erased entirely, so a session could not
    change model. `style.js` restores that node when it is the only copy and
    anchors it to the send button (right wing, bottom row) instead of the 0.1.1
    clone slot in the left wing.
11. Header controls: the Fairy controls are placed before the stock header
    buttons (owner request) with the header's 8px rhythm, and the blank-session
    fallback toggle stops short of the 0.2.1 header-corner button instead of
    covering it.
12. Mascot preferences (`mascotScale`, `mascotAnimationSpeed`) are part of the
    stored schema; the first port dropped them on write, which silently reset the
    scale slider after every drag.
13. Header control sizing and glyphs: the three Fairy header controls are rendered
    as 28x28 ghost icon buttons (8px radius, 16px glyph) to match the stock header
    buttons, with their labels moved to `aria-label`/`title`; the blank-session
    fallback borrows the stock corner button's top edge for vertical alignment;
    and the day/night crescent is drawn as a single even SVG path instead of the
    reference's 1.7px border with a transparent top edge (Chrome rounds border
    widths per side, which rendered that arc with an uneven stroke).

